        },
        "etag" : "\"Q44G99shyMl14lSVN9oTpl4EamI/Qde9ahx610y0Tm1KnwDiozPGu6A\"",
        "id" : "z131yn3jvov1s3ipp04cexrqywbvcrqgizk0k.1344024034150423",
        "kind" : "plus#comment",
        "object" : {
          "content" : "I usually cut the legs off a spare cap or resistor and have that run the trace lines.  I cut and bend them to fit the trace I am trying to make, and the wires make it easy to get the solder and pads to stick.  I am also using am much better solder station that has digital controls. ~350 degrees seems to be the right temp for me. <br /><br />Lately I have been buying the proto-boards with the square pads at <span class=\"proflinkWrapper\"><span class=\"proflinkPrefix\">+</span><a class=\"proflink\" href=\"https://plus.google.com/100139456300784928828\" oid=\"100139456300784928828\">RadioShack</a></span>. They don&#39;t come in the full-sized boards but I can usually get all of my stuff on the boards that they do have with the square pads.  I find that square pads solder a lot better because they have more pad and less space between them. ",
          "objectType" : "comment"
        },
        "plusoners" : {
          "totalItems" : 0
        },
